-- title:
--   Lifts of residual eigensystems give points of T_θ
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ (i.e. `NeZero N`) and a set $S$ of natural numbers, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Let $\theta \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ be a ring homomorphism to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Assume `HasIntegralStructure N 2`: the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3), spanned by those weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers, is the whole space. Finally let $\chi \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}$ be a ring homomorphism whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ is $\theta$, i.e. `IsLocalRing.residue 𝒪 (χ t) = θ t` for every $t$. Then there exists an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from `heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ` — the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` at the submonoid obtained as the image under `latticeBaseChange N S 𝒪` of the prime complement of `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ` — to $\mathcal{O}$ such that $\psi(\pi(t)) = \chi(t)$ for all $t \in \mathbb{T}$, where $\pi$ is the structure map `heckeLocal.π N S 𝒪 θ`.
--
--   This is the point-counting half of the universal property of the local Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T}_\theta$ attached to a residual eigensystem $\theta$: every $\mathcal{O}$-valued eigensystem congruent to $\theta$ factors through $\mathbb{T}_\theta$. No uniqueness of $\psi$ is asserted, and no $\chi$ is produced. It is used in the construction of the Hecke coefficient ring and of the Galois representation data attached to $\theta$, notably by [`CuspForm.exists_heckeCoefficientRing_of_hasIntegralStructure`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_heckeCoefficientRing_of_hasIntegralStructure) and the lemmas producing $\pi$-adic and ordinary specialisations from prime-factor conditions.
